her for quite a while  because they are members of the same  squad but both austin yami can read  key and this very rare ability allows  them to work together in a way that  other mages who can't read ki just  wouldn't be able to do  at least that is my opinion the fight  rages on and dante continues to take  damage from yami  but he also continues to dodge direct  hits from asta  which allows him to keep regenerating at  this point we get some really really  good battle panels  in the manga but before you know it  asta's limit for using his true demon  power  runs down to only 8 seconds and so  asta attempts to end the fight by  summoning his demon dweller sword  dante prevents asta from using the demon  dweller sword by wrapping osta  up in his grotesque flesh magic asta  then summons the demon destroyer sword  right out of his grimoire but dante is  able to disrupt asta's attack  yet again after a new attack from yami  dante regenerates yet again  and there are now only three seconds  left before asta has to relinquish his  true demon power  so he is quickly running out of options  at the very last moment  with like a single second left dante  throws his  own katana over to asta asta grabs the  sword with his right hand  encases the sword in anti-magic and  delivers  a direct kessagiri cut to dante's body  by the way asta's kesagiri form is  surprisingly good for someone who has  presumably never used a katana  let alone studied iaido or kendo but hey  let's go with it everyone is stunned as  dante's body  suddenly reverts back to his normal  human form  and the crown flies off his head as a  dark scar  made of anti-magic runs down the side of  his torso  the end of the chapter suggests that  yami and asta have won  and that dante has been defeated  although  personally i wouldn't rush to judgement  just yet  this was definitely an excellent battle  i loved the teamwork between yami and  asta  and i loved the fact that asta was able  to unleash the true power  of his demon but i still wouldn't be  surprised if dante  somehow survives this after all the  times we've seen dante regenerate  i won't make any speculations about his  death or defeat until we have official  confirmation  we also can't forget that his demon  lucifer  is one of the strongest high ranked  demons so who knows what he is still  capable of doing  let's say the dante really is done for  does that necessarily mean  that lucifer is also defeated or  could the demon still cling to this  world and potentially possess  another host i just don't see a high  ranked demon with a name  as important as lucifer going down so  easily  but hey you never know so we'll have to  wait and see  what did you guys think about aston  yami's teamwork and do you think that  using yami's sword allowed asta to  actually  mix dark magic and anti-magic during his  attack  or was it just anti-magic that  ultimately hit dante  i think that the whole asta needing to  use yami's sword was a really nice touch  by tabata  and i really enjoyed that moment a  moment that showcased the great trust  and camaraderie that these two  characters have and  since these are literally my two  favorite characters in the entire series  i absolutely loved seeing this finally  i want to ask you guys something so feel  free to share your thoughts down in the  comments  below what do you think will be the  consequences for asta's decision to use  true demon power  even if it was only for a few seconds  will this deal with the devil now give  more control of his body to the demon  will he lose control of that arm in the  long run  will his personality change because of  the demon  it seems that whenever in fiction any  sort of deal with the devil is made  there are always very real consequences  so i'm very curious to see  what will happen to asta now will the  anti-magic demon just be like oh i like  you asta  so it's all good fam or will we see some  real consequences for asta in the long  term  let me 